WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.684 --> 00:00:02.312
- [Reporter] Nylon stockings make me think

00:00:02.312 --> 00:00:05.486
of Melanie Griffith in Working Girl.

00:00:05.486 --> 00:00:07.721
But they actually have
an interesting past,

00:00:07.721 --> 00:00:09.893
and it involves the U.S. Army,

00:00:09.893 --> 00:00:13.226
gravy juice, and department store riots.

00:00:15.198 --> 00:00:19.569
Until the 1930s, women wore
silk and nylon stockings,

00:00:19.569 --> 00:00:23.314
because having your legs
uncovered was not acceptable.

00:00:23.314 --> 00:00:25.098
But then World War II happened.

00:00:25.098 --> 00:00:28.027
The U.S. military began
buying up nylon and silk

00:00:28.027 --> 00:00:31.492
and using it to make
parachutes and tires and cords.

00:00:31.492 --> 00:00:34.733
So women donated their
stockings to the war effort.

00:00:34.733 --> 00:00:36.981
The official motto for
women during World War II

00:00:36.981 --> 00:00:38.894
was "make do and mend.”

00:00:38.894 --> 00:00:40.292
Wartime ads told women

00:00:40.292 --> 00:00:42.615
that they needed to keep up appearances.

00:00:42.615 --> 00:00:45.983
So, when life gave them
lemons, women in the '40s,

00:00:45.983 --> 00:00:48.233
they made liquid stockings.

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:53.140
It was a makeup for your legs,
kind of like self-tanner.

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:55.702
It looked like stockings if applied well.

00:00:55.702 --> 00:00:59.242
Women even drew the seam line
on the back of their calves.

00:00:59.242 --> 00:01:01.414
And this was not easy.

00:01:01.414 --> 00:01:04.302
Some salons offered it as a service.

00:01:04.302 --> 00:01:06.474
But if this foundation wasn't around,

00:01:06.474 --> 00:01:08.927
women used gravy juice.

00:01:08.927 --> 00:01:12.227
That brownish hue mimicked
the color of liquid stockings,

00:01:12.227 --> 00:01:13.144
and worked.

00:01:14.745 --> 00:01:16.711
Soon after the end of World War II,

00:01:16.711 --> 00:01:19.624
DuPont, the big name in
stocking manufacturing,

00:01:19.624 --> 00:01:22.622
said they would be producing
women's nylons again.

00:01:22.622 --> 00:01:25.009
And in 1946, a store
in Pittsburgh announced

00:01:25.009 --> 00:01:27.006
that finally they had them.

00:01:27.006 --> 00:01:29.278
Roughly 40,000 women showed up

00:01:29.278 --> 00:01:32.689
only to find out 13,000
pairs were available.

00:01:32.689 --> 00:01:35.692
Fighting ensued, and 1946 became known

00:01:35.692 --> 00:01:38.682
as the year of the Nylon Riots.

00:01:38.682 --> 00:01:40.979
Obviously, DuPont got their act together.

00:01:40.979 --> 00:01:43.924
And by the end of that year,
the nylon depression ended.

00:01:43.924 --> 00:01:46.521
And out went the gravy tights.

00:01:46.521 --> 00:01:47.771
Thank goodness.

